  "description": "Reusable .NET 10 package that wraps ASP.NET Core Identity with cookie and JWT auth, Google OAuth, a pluggable e-mail provider, a multi-tenant model with dynamic RBAC (roles + module permissions), and secure defaults — wired up with a single AddMyIdentity call. JWT and Google OAuth secrets are supplied by the consumer (never shipped in the package).",
  "id": "MyIdentity",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-10-16T18:54:08.71Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "vBwuTAzuKb2RLcCSZiuNy4yTO4s8W/BRuYNHbCjZc4QdT2/A+oLO9Q2gjE72X1+xpTGZmeqXXJdavzVuM/mo4w==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 609371,
  "published": "2026-10-16T18:42:00.27Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.3.0: self-registration becomes an explicit decision of every application. New required option MyIdentity:Authentication:AllowSelfRegistration (bool?, MyIdentityAuthenticationOptions.AllowSelfRegistration), with no default: an application that does not declare it, in configuration or from configureOptions, does not start. With anything but true, the anonymous RegisterAsync and every registration that carries an external identity (the Google callback, or the server overload with a MyIdentityExternalRegistration) are refused before anything is written: RegisterAsync throws MyIdentityErrorCodes.SelfRegistrationDisabled, and the Google callback returns false whatever AuthenticationProperties.Items[\"RegisterIfNotExist\"] says (audit reason RegistrationDisabled). Not governed: IMyIdentityUserService.CreateAsync, the bootstrap SystemAdmin and the server overload without an external identity. Adds MyIdentityMessageDescriber.SelfRegistrationDisabled. Upgrading from 5.2.0: MyIdentity/UPGRADE.md §47.",
